.TH FORMWATCH 1 "formwatch" "formwatch"
.SH NAME
formwatch \- test public-service forms for broken flows, accessibility, mobile usability, and lost input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B formwatch
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B formwatch
drives a headless Chrome browser against a form, runs a set of checks
(submission flow, accessibility via axe-core, mobile usability,
validation errors, required documents, autofill hints, input persistence,
bot-protection detection, and passive vulnerability scanning), records
the result, and reports what changed since the previous run.
.PP
.B Only point formwatch at forms you own or are explicitly authorized to
test.
Automated access to third-party systems may be unlawful and can violate
their terms of service. Run
.B formwatch legal
for the full notice, or read
.IR docs/legal.md .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init \fR[\fIPATH\fR]
Scaffold a starter forms.yml and an example custom check.
.TP
.B test \fIURL\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Run every check against a single form. Supports --json, --junit, --sarif,
and --out.
.TP
.B monitor \fIforms.yml\fR...
Run every form listed in one or more YAML configs. Supports --json,
--junit, --sarif, --shard, and --out.
.TP
.B watch \fIforms.yml\fR... [\fB--interval-secs\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--max-cycles\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--json\fR|\fB--junit\fR|\fB--sarif\fR|\fB--csv\fR] [\fB--out\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Re-run monitor on a schedule (default every 300s) until Ctrl+C, printing
a one-line summary per cycle and full detail only for breaching runs.
With an export flag, stdout carries only the per-cycle artifact instead
(--json emits one compact object per cycle, i.e. JSONL; --out files are
overwritten each pass). Failed cycles are retried next cycle; Ctrl+C
stops cleanly.
.TP
.B vuln \fIURL\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Scan one form for common passive vulnerabilities only (insecure
transport, form data protection, security headers, cookie security,
information disclosure). No attack payloads are ever sent. Supports
--json and --min-severity \fIlow\fR|\fImedium\fR|\fIhigh\fR|\fIcritical\fR.
.TP
.B report \fR[\fB--html\fR|\fB--json\fR|\fB--junit\fR|\fB--sarif\fR|\fB--prometheus\fR|\fB--markdown\fR] [\fB--out\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Render the latest run of every known form.
.TP
.B validate \fR[\fIforms.yml\fR...] [\fB--probe\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Lint registries without launching a browser. Exits 1 on errors.
With --probe, also GETs each valid URL and reports reachability.
.TP
.B trends \fR[\fB--last-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--min-pass-rate\fR \fIR\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Pass-rate, current status, and streaks per form over history.
--min-pass-rate exits 1 when any form falls below it.
.TP
.B flakes \fR[\fB--json\fR]
Checks that keep flip-flopping (2+ transitions). Exits 1 when any exist.
.TP
.B diff \fITARGET\fR [\fB--json\fR]
What changed between a form's last two runs (URL or display name).
.TP
.B history \fITARGET\fR [\fB--last-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
A form's recorded runs, newest last.
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB--format\fR \fIjsonl\fR|\fIjson\fR|\fIcsv\fR] [\fB--out\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Dump full history (every run of every form).
.TP
.B sitemap \fIURL\fR [\fB--max-urls\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--check-forms\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Discover candidate form pages from a sitemap URL or a site root
(robots.txt plus /sitemap.xml).
.TP
.B ci \fR[\fB--forms\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB--schedule\fR \fICRON\fR] [\fB--out\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Write a starter GitHub Actions workflow that validates then monitors.
.TP
.B legal
Print the authorized-use notice.
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\fB--json\fR] [\fB--probe-llm\fR]
Check the local environment (Chrome, writable dirs, config) without
running a form; exits non-zero if something a run needs is broken.
With --probe-llm, also probe the configured LLM provider's connectivity
and credentials.
.TP
.B notify-test \fR[\fB--webhook-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Send one synthetic regression to verify a webhook is reachable.
.TP
.B baseline \fR[\fB--write\fR] [\fB--out\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Generate a baseline of accepted findings from history (--write), or print
the configured/current one.
.TP
.B serve \fR[\fB--addr\fR \fIHOST:PORT\fR] [\fB--api-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR]
Serve read-only HTTP endpoints (/healthz, /readyz, /metrics, /api/forms,
/api/summary, /api/trends, /api/flakes, /badge.svg) over the accumulated
history.
Binds to 127.0.0.1:8080 by default. With --api-token (or serve_api_token
/ FORMWATCH_SERVE_API_TOKEN), data endpoints require
Authorization: Bearer <token>; the probes stay open.
.TP
.B audit \fR[\fB--verify\fR] [\fB--show\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Inspect the tamper-evident audit log: --verify recomputes its hash chain
(exit 1 when broken), --show N prints the last N entries.
.TP
.B prune \fR(\fB--keep-last\fR \fIN\fR | \fB--keep-days\fR \fID\fR) [\fB--dry-run\fR]
Delete old history runs, keeping the most recent ones.
.TP
.B demo \fR[\fB--addr\fR \fIHOST:PORT\fR]
Serve a bundled demo site of deliberately varied forms on 127.0.0.1:8099
for trying formwatch without touching a third-party site.
.TP
.B completions \fISHELL\fR
Emit a shell completion script (bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config \fIPATH\fR
Load settings from a config file.
.TP
.B --history-dir \fIDIR\fR
Where run history is stored (default: .formwatch/history).
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Increase diagnostic verbosity (repeatable).
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Only log errors.
.TP
.B --log-format \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR
Diagnostic log format on stderr.
.TP
.B --accept-terms
Acknowledge the authorized-use notice (required for --submit).
.TP
.B --no-screenshots
Do not capture screenshots on non-Pass checks.
.TP
.B --proxy \fIURL\fR / --insecure / --no-sandbox
Chrome network and sandbox controls.
.TP
.B --audit-log \fIFILE\fR
Append one JSON audit line per run.
.TP
.B --baseline \fIFILE\fR
JSON baseline of accepted findings; only new or worsened findings fail.
.TP
.B --per-host-delay-ms \fIMS\fR / --max-concurrent \fIN\fR / --check-timeout-secs \fISECS\fR
Pacing and timeout controls.
.TP
.B --retries \fIN\fR / --max-load-ms \fIMS\fR
Retry page-load failures with backoff (default 0); fail forms slower
than the load budget via a synthetic Load budget check.
.TP
.B --shard \fIINDEX/TOTAL\fR
Check only a deterministic slice of the configured forms (e.g. 2/5), for
splitting a large registry across CI jobs.
.TP
.B --fail-on \fIfail\fR|\fIwarn\fR
Which status makes the process exit non-zero (default: fail).
.TP
.B --skip-vuln
Skip the passive vulnerability checks (insecure transport, form data
protection, security headers, information disclosure).
.TP
.B --llm
Enable the optional LLM semantic checks of error and instruction wording.
Page text (redacted, truncated) is sent to the configured provider.
.TP
.B --llm-provider \fIopenai\fR|\fIanthropic\fR|\fImock\fR, --llm-model \fIMODEL\fR, --llm-base-url \fIURL\fR
Provider selection and endpoint (use --llm-base-url for OpenAI-compatible
or self-hosted models).
.TP
.B --llm-api-key \fIKEY\fR
API key (prefer the provider's environment variable, e.g. OPENAI_API_KEY).
.TP
.B --llm-threshold \fIN\fR, --llm-fail, --llm-max-retries \fIN\fR, --llm-no-redact, --llm-no-cache
Pass bar (1-5, default 3), whether a low score fails, transient-failure
retries, and privacy/cache controls.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if no check returned FAIL; 1 if any check did (or a config failed to
parse); 2 if --submit was refused for lack of acknowledgement.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full notice: docs/legal.md. Project: https://github.com/voidstackloop/formwatch
